# Answer key: romeo_juliet.txt
#
# Source: reconstructed from Project Gutenberg #1513, preserving its exact
# apparatus, contents list, Dramatis Personae and heading conventions. The
# act and scene bodies are abbreviated; the structure is faithful.
#
# The judgements worth stating explicitly:
#
#   - Lines 25-57 are a table of CONTENTS. They list acts and scenes that
#     appear again later. They are front matter, not the start of the play.
#   - Line 69-70 begins "SCENE. During the greater part of the Play in
#     Verona" and is prose within Dramatis Personae, not a scene heading.
#   - THE PROLOGUE is spoken by Chorus and precedes ACT I. Editions differ on
#     whether it belongs to the play; here it is marked front matter, on the
#     grounds that a corpus of the drama proper begins at ACT I.
#   - The play itself begins at line 82.

1-19     pg_header      Gutenberg header, metadata block, START marker
21-23    front_matter   Title and byline
25-57    front_matter   Contents
59-70    front_matter   Dramatis Personae, including the SCENE prose note
72-80    front_matter   THE PROLOGUE
82-238   body           ACT I through ACT V
240-248  pg_licence     END marker and licence text
